    "md5": "4d14d17c84f0a398e23293de4cc32f07",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1854,
    "chunk_text": "Vice Admiral Damian Fernando assumes office as new Navy Commander\n\nColombo, July 1 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake promoted the Chief of Staff of the Sri Lanka Navy, Rear Admiral Damian Fernando to the 3 star rank of Vice Admiral and appointed him as the 27th Commander of the Sri Lanka Navy with effect from 01 Jul 26.\n\nIn a symbolic gesture of handing over command, the outgoing Navy Commander Admiral Kanchana Banagoda presented the Admiral's Sword to the newly appointed Commander of the Navy, Vice Admiral Damian Fernando at the Navy Headquarters. Subsequently, Vice Admiral Damian Fernando was accorded a 48 - member Guard of Honour, marked by time-honoured naval traditions. The newly appointed Navy Commander commenced his official duties amidst the chanting of blessings and religious observances from all faiths, invoking success for his tenure ahead.\n\nVice Admiral Fernando joined the Executive Branch of the Sri Lanka Navy as an Officer Cadet of the 21st Intake in 1991 after completing his education at the St. Joseph Vaz College, Wennapuwa. Upon successfully completing his initial naval training at the Naval and Maritime Academy, Trincomalee, he was commissioned as a Sub Lieutenant in 1993.\n\nThroughout his distinguished naval career, Vice Admiral Fernando has completed a wide range of professional military education and specialist training programmes both in Sri Lanka and overseas. These include the Long Gunnery and Missile Course at INS Dronacharya, India (2003), the Naval Weapons Engineering Course in China (2010), and the Royal College of Defence Studies (RCDS) Programme in the United Kingdom.\n\nAn accomplished scholar, he holds a Master's Degree in Defence Studies from General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and a Master's Degree in International Security and Strategy from King's College London."
