    "chunk_size_bytes": 1039,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka highlights climate action and SDG integration in Bangkok\n\nColombo, July 02 (Daily Mirror) - Deputy Minister of Environment Anton Jayakody has reaffirmed Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to implementing the Paris Agreement and the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development during his address at the Seventh Global Conference on Climate and SDG Synergies held in Bangkok on 29\u201330 June 2026.\n\nSpeaking at the high-level segment titled \u201cRecommitting to the Paris Agreement and the 2030 Agenda: Regaining Peace, Solidarity, Sustainability and Prosperity,\u201d the Deputy Minister emphasized Sri Lanka\u2019s integrated policy approach to climate action and sustainable development.\n\nHe outlined national priorities under Sri Lanka\u2019s updated Nationally Determined Contribution, including renewable energy expansion, sustainable transport systems, circular economy development, ecosystem restoration and climate resilience. He also called for increased climate finance, technology transfer and capacity-building support for developing countries."
