    "md5": "896bb6ce7a0e2c3d317f6d45110529f8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1323,
    "chunk_text": "Sajith Premadasa congratulates Communist Party of China on 105th anniversary\n\nColombo, July 02 (Daily Mirror) - In a special message marking the 105th anniversary of the Communist Party of China (CPC), Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa extended his warm congratulations, commending the Party\u2019s remarkable transformation and its contribution to China\u2019s emergence as a global economic and technological powerhouse.\n\nPremadasa praised the CPC\u2019s commitment to economic reform, modernization, innovation, and inclusive growth, noting that its development model has enabled China to achieve shared prosperity while promoting social equity and fairness. He said Sri Lanka has valuable lessons to learn from China\u2019s development experience, particularly its reform and opening-up policies and steadfast commitment to implementation.\n\nHe also emphasized the importance of peaceful coexistence and cooperation in Asia, expressing hope for the continued strong relationship between China and India as key drivers of regional and global progress.\n\nHighlighting similarities between the CPC\u2019s modern economic approach and the principles of the Samagi Jana Balawegaya, Premadasa reaffirmed his commitment to strengthening party-to-party cooperation and further enhancing the longstanding friendship between Sri Lanka and China."
