    "md5": "569158bdd38fc86cbdc4647b0fc3f5e1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1816,
    "chunk_text": "SLIIT\u2019s SciFest 2026 inspires next generation of scientists and innovators\n\nThe Department of Applied Sciences at the Faculty of Humanities and Sciences, SLIIT, successfully hosted SciFest 2026 on 5th June at the SLIIT Malabe Campus.\n\nThis annual science festival was designed to inspire both school and university students to explore the fields of science, innovation, and entrepreneurship as key drivers of real-world solutions.\n\nThe fourth edition of SciFest brought together approximately 300 participants, including school students, university undergraduates, academics, industry experts, and partners. Organized in collaboration with the Ministry of Education, the event highlighted SLIIT\u2019s ongoing commitment to advancing science education, fostering innovation, and strengthening ties between academia and industry.\n\nThe occasion was graced by Dr. Ruchira Wijesena, Senior Lecturer at the Institute of Technology, University of Moratuwa, as the Chief Guest and keynote speaker. Distinguished attendees included Prof. Lakshman Ratnayake, Chancellor and Chairman; Prof. Nimal Rajapakse, Senior Deputy Vice-Chancellor and Provost; Dr. Malitha Wijesundara, Pro Vice-Chancellor, Faculty of Humanities and Sciences; Prof. Ayantha Gomes, Dean, Faculty of Engineering; Prof. Colin N. Peiris, Dean, Academic Development and Quality Assurance; and Prof. Sriyani N. Peiris, former Head of the Department of Applied Sciences.\n\nThe judging panel comprised respected industry and academic professionals, including Dr. Lasantha Malavige, Chairman of Lassana Group; Dr. Dilan Fernando, Director of SLIIT Innovate; Niresh Ratnagopal, Head of Programs at Hatch Works (Pvt) Ltd.; Rishan Sampath, Manager of Dilmah Conservation & Sustainability; along with Prof. Eranga Wijesinghe and Prof. Nathali Silva representing SLIIT."
