    "chunk_text": "I thought that the problem had ended there. I was wrong. Months later I visited Singapore with my friend for a holiday. There, she had contacted a South Indian acquaintance who invited us for dinner. He did not take us to his apartment in a working class high-rise but seated us at a table in a food court attached to his building and ordered several bottles of beer\u2014large and warm, and food. I warned my friend not to drink as I suspected the intentions of the man.\n\nShe had arranged with a travel agent friend to send workers to Singapore. The agent in Singapore who took the money, had not met the workers at Singapore airport and the airline sent them back to Sri Lanka. The travel agent had sued my friend for the money for the air tickets. That case was settled later out of court, and our romance blossomed.\n\nAfter my holiday in Sri Lanka, I flew from Colombo to Karachi and from there arrived at Dhahran Airport on a flight of Pakistan International Airlines (PIA). The head of the Department of Mechanical Engineering of the Saudi University had come to the airport to meet me. First, he took me to the house that had been assigned to me, where I left my belongings, and from there, he took me to the university.\n\nThe university land was vast, just as I had read in the manual. There were trees newly planted in fresh soil, tall date palms, and massive concrete buildings. There were also neatly arranged and modern staff quarters and a well-planned road network. On one side, I could see the Arabian Sea, part of the mighty Indian Ocean. The scorching heat could not be eased even by the sight of water. The buildings and vehicles were air-conditioned, which was a blessing. Whenever a slight breeze passed, fine sand would rise and enter my nostrils, mouth, ears, and eyes."
