    "chunk_text": "In the private sector you are free of all these. They are interested in results, not in processes or polemics. Nobody disturbs you or tells you what to do. You could always talk to people if you want to. But that is up to you. Otherwise you just do what you have to do. Nobody is really bothered as to whether you did your work in an office, in the car, at home, or over lunch or dinner at a hotel or at the sea beach. What matters is the result.\n\nMy private sector engagements were supplemented by other part time responsibilities in the university sector, the public sector itself on a part time basis, some regional responsibilities as well as certain on going responsibilities in the broad social sector. Retirement therefore, had led to a varied range of productive work devoid of serious stress.\n\n(Next week a round up of what I had said about the Minister and relate briefly what it was like to work with the President)\n\n(Excerpted from In Pursuit of Governance, autobiography of MDD Pieris)\n\nCentral bank gold holdings are at a 50year high. What\u2019s behind the jump in\u00a0reserves?\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
