    "language": "en",
    "md5": "265bdee0410b644aec1e071406d58251",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1624,
    "chunk_text": "Premadasa became the likely right wing candidate to contest the forthcoming Presidential election though Ranil was prevaricating without giving him the nomination. At this stage Sirisena inducted me as the Chairman of the National Security Council which was the apex body in charge of coordinating intelligence regarding national security. Ranil, an ex-officio member, had stopped attending and we were very much on our own.\n\nLater there was an explosion in a coconut estate in Eastern province where the Zaharan group practiced detonating bombs. The villagers of Kattankudy had complained several times that this extremist group living within their midst was prone to violence and were creating trouble. They had assaulted the local religious dignitaries who had complained to the police and senior administrative authorities. But nothing was done because it now appears that some of the perpetrators were paid informers of army intelligence who could not be exposed.\n\nWhen the police were hot on the trail of the Zaharan gang, army intelligence operatives had asked them to call off the hunt. Not many in our Security Council had even visited Kattankudy which was the epicenter of the violence prone Islamists. Since I had done demographic research in Kattankudy many years earlier I was more familiar with the terrain and social conditions of the village than many of the top sleuths in the Security Council. I knew for instance that being traders, the Muslims of Kattankudy had an all island network of contacts. Zaharan could easily activate it in places like Mawanella, Kuliyapitiya and Gampola as it later transpired."
  },
