    "chunk_size_bytes": 1567,
    "chunk_text": "Eric served as Government Agent Trincomalee sometime later. This was at a time of civil disturbance in most parts of the island. District Coordinating Officers were appointed to many districts. In almost all cases these were Military officers, placed above the civilian Government Agents. The one exception was Eric who was appointed the Coordinating Officer for Trincomalee district. Most likely this was due to his previous experience in the Ministry of Defence. Eric later served as the Head of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration (SLIDA).\n\nIn conclusion, let me add a personal note. Eric and I joined Mahinda College Galle in 1947 and we were there until 1954. Then from 1955 to 1958, we were at the University of Ceylon, Peradeniya and at Ramanathan Hall. Both of us read for a degree in Economics. Much later in life, when I had returned from a period of 30 years abroad, we connected with each other. Our teacher and mentor at Mahinda College in the 1950s had been the late C.G.L. (Cadmus) Samarasinghe, who had been a great influence in our lives. He was then living in retirement at his rural home in Baddegama (near Galle). Almost every half year, we visited him, along with a few contemporary friends, to spend the day, and reminisce on our life and times.\n\nCentral bank gold holdings are at a 50year high. What\u2019s behind the jump in\u00a0reserves?\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
