    "md5": "36cb035b5f50fa7915707f405fe242b5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1471,
    "chunk_text": "Babar back as captain as Pakistan name upcoming Test squads\n\nICC - Former skipper Babar Azam has been named to return as captain as Pakistan revealed their Test squads for upcoming ICC World Test Championship assignments against the West Indies and England.\n\nBabar replaces Shan Masood in the role and will lead the side for two Test in the Caribbean from July 25 and a trio of Tests in England from August 19 as part of the ongoing World Test Championship.\n\nFour uncapped players are included in the squads, with left-arm spinner Ali Usman, right-handed batter Muhammad Awais Zafar, right-arm fast bowler Ubaid Shah and wicket-keeper-batter Muhammad Ghazi Ghori all in contention for their first Test cap.\n\nSaud Shakeel is in the squad for the England series, subject to proving his fitness prior the series.\n\nPakistan currently sit in ninth place on the World Test Championship standings.\n\nPakistan squad for West Indies: Babar Azam (c), Aamir Jamal, Abdullah Fazal, Ali Usman, Azan Awais, Imam ul Haq, Khurram Shahzad, Mohammad Abbas, Mohammad Ali, Mohammad Rizwan, Mohammad Awais Zafar, Muhammad Ghazi Ghori, Sajid Khan, Salman Ali Agha, Shan Masood, Ubaid Shah\n\nPakistan squad for England: Babar Azam (c), Aamir Jamal, Abdullah Fazal, Ali Usman, Azan Awais, Imam ul Haq, Khurram Shahzad, Mohammad Abbas, Mohammad Ali, Mohammad Rizwan, Muhammad Awais Zafar, Muhammad Ghazi Ghori, Sajid Khan, Salman Ali Agha, Saud Shakeel (subject to fitness), Shan Masood, Ubaid Shah"
  },
