    "md5": "085177f54dbd73d3e8a67bc82b5d5d83",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1282,
    "chunk_text": "The session was attended by IDL Deputy Chairperson Indhu Selvaratnam, members of the senior leadership team and the wider management team, a testament to the strong demand among Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate leadership for the insights Nathavitharana offers.\n\nCommenting on the impact of the session, IDL Chief Executive Officer Janek Jayasekara said: \u201cLeadership today is no longer defined by individual brilliance alone; it is shaped by how effectively our teams collaborate, trust one another and move towards shared goals. Vidusha\u2019s session on Collective Leadership reaffirmed something we deeply believe in at IDL: that sustainable growth comes from empowering our people to lead together, not in isolation. We are grateful for the depth of insight he brought to our leadership team, and we remain firmly committed to providing our leaders with platforms such as this, as we continue building an organisation that is agile, resilient and future ready.\u201d\n\nIDL\u2019s engagement of Nathavitharana for its Guest Lecture Series reflects the strong impression he continues to make on organisations he works with, and reinforces his standing as a trusted partner for companies seeking to strengthen leadership capability through contemporary management thinking and global best practice."
