    "md5": "6a0ad47f265afb2c960fbec04d1040f4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1106,
    "chunk_text": "Five children among 6 killed, in Mumbai chawl collapse\n\nTHE HINDU - Five children among six persons were killed in a house collapse in Mumbai\u2019s Mankhurd area amid heavy rains on Sunday (July 5, 2026) night, officials said.\n\nAccording to the BMC, when two to three tenements forming part of the three-storey structure collapsed at Janata Nagar chawl at 8.30 p.m. on Sunday (July 5, 2026).\n\nTeams of the Mumbai Fire Brigade, police, BMC\u2019s Ward Staff and ambulance were pressed into service. The injured were rescued and moved to Rajawadi Hospital and Shatabdi Hospital.\n\nAccording to the information provided by Shatabdi Hospital, five persons brought in were declared dead.\n\nThey included a 32-year-old woman and four children aged between two and 14 years. According to the information given by Rajawadi Hospital, the condition of a 24-year-old man is stable.\n\nChief Minister Devendra Fadnavis has expressed deep grief over the tragic incident. Stating that the government shares the grief of the bereaved families, he has announced financial assistance of \u20b95 lakh to the next of kin of the deceased."
  },
