    "chunk_size_bytes": 1560,
    "chunk_text": "Inmates to be transferred following deadly Negombo Prison riot\n\nColombo, July 06 (Daily Mirror) - Authorities have begun arrangements to transfer a group of inmates from Negombo Prison to other prisons across the country following the deadly unrest at the facility.\n\nPrison Media Spokesperson and Commissioner of Prisons, A.C. Gajanayake, said the transfers are part of urgent measures aimed at easing tensions inside the prison and restoring order.\n\nAt least 25 fatalities, including five prison officers and 20 inmates, were reported following the clash at Negombo Prison.\n\nFurthermore, nearly 100 individuals sustained injuries during the encounter. While most are receiving emergency treatment locally, eight critically injured victims have been transferred to the National Hospital of Sri Lanka in Colombo for specialised medical care.\n\nThe latest unrest erupted around 10:00 a.m. today when a group of inmates allegedly attempted to force their way through the prison\u2019s main entrance in an apparent bid to break out.\n\nPolice and the Police Special Task Force (STF) were deployed to the prison to bring the situation under control. Witnesses reported hearing multiple gunshots from within the prison premises as security forces worked to suppress the violence.\n\nLater, the Army and Air Force were also deployed to ease the situation.\n\n16 injured in Negombo Prison clash; STF deployed to restore order\n\nUpdate: Two prisoners killed, over 25 injured in Negombo Prison violence\n\nFemale inmates stage rooftop protest following deadly clash at Negombo Prison"
