    "chunk_text": "Negombo prison clash: Inmates moved to Bogambara\n\nColombo, July 6 (Daily Mirror) - A group of inmates from Negombo Prison has been transferred to the Bogambara Open Air Prison in Pallekele, Kandy, following escalating violence inside the facility.\n\nThe transfer comes after a clash between two groups of inmates at the Negombo Prison, prompting authorities to move a section of prisoners to another correctional facility as a security measure.\n\nPolice said the confrontation occurred between remand prisoners and convicted inmates held at the prison.\n\nMeanwhile, the death toll from the incident has risen to 26.\n\nJustice Minister Attorney-at-Law Harshana Nanayakkara, speaking to the media, said seven prison officers were among those killed in the unrest.\n\nNo casualties among foreign inmates in Negombo prison clash: Authorities"
