    "chunk_text": "World scene for Sri Lankan Reggae\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s reggae heartbeat is back on the road, and it has been a busy run since last September, 2025.\n\nYes, JAYASRI are spending their summer 2026 commitments in Europe with the full band, carrying the sound of home to stages across the globe.\n\nRohitha and Rohan of JAYASRI spent time in Sri Lanka, between international tours, touching down in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom, Japan, Malaysia, South Korea, Dubai and Oman.\n\n\u201cThe Sri Lanka shows were packed, loud, and full of that special energy you only get performing for your own people,\u201d says Rohitha.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s always great and full of fun to perform for our people in packed venues, and gratitude goes out to every fan, organiser, backing band and crew member who made those nights happen.\u201d\n\nA standout moment came in Colombo, where JAYASRI received the Legendary Icons of Sri Lankan Reggae and World Music Award at the Platinum Excellence Awards 2026.\n\nThe band members say having won international honours in Europe before, bringing a major award home, to the motherland, made it even more meaningful.\n\nNow Europe calls again and JAYASRI returns for the festival season, with a headline stop at Austria\u2019s ONE LOVE REGGAE FESTIVAL 2026, on the 7th and 8th August, in Wiesen.\n\nIt\u2019s one of the biggest reggae gatherings on the continent, and JAYASRI will be sharing the bill with legends like Alpha Blondy and Solar System, The Wailers, Alborosie and Shengen Clan, Culture, Dawn Penn, The Congos, Christopher Ellis and more.\n\nThis beautiful reggae festival is set in nature, with camping, food stalls, DJs, a DUB club, drumming, art, yoga, kids\u2019 zones and workshops; it\u2019s reggae the way it was meant to be felt, says Rohitha.\n\nLast Saturday (4th), JAYASRI did their thing with WAYO at the YAMAYA CONCERT, held at the prestigious Indigo, at The O2, in London.\n\nThey will also join WAYO\u2019s European run on 11th July in Brescia, and 18th July in Naples, Italy."
