    "chunk_size_bytes": 1350,
    "chunk_text": "Namal-led group launches \u201cA Team \u2013 Next Wave\u201d\n\nColombo, July 7 (Daily Mirror) - Opposition MPs Namal Rajapaksa, Rohitha Abeygunawardena, Anuradha Jayaratne, D. V. Chanaka and Chanaka Madugoda on Tuesday launched a new political platform titled \u201cA Team \u2013 Next Wave\u201d, saying it aims to unite opposition voices both inside and outside Parliament.\n\nThe MPs said the platform seeks to provide representation for political parties, independent groups and individuals who are not adequately represented in Parliament due to the government\u2019s overwhelming majority.\n\nThey said the initiative would work with opposition MPs, political groups and other stakeholders without parliamentary representation to raise public concerns on national issues.\n\nThe MPs added that the platform is expected to bring together representatives from various opposition parties and independent groups to build a broader political alliance.\n\nThey said the country currently needs an experienced political team capable of addressing challenges faced by the public, including economic hardships, the tax burden, and issues affecting farmers, fishermen, graduates, youth and students.\n\nThe MPs said the long-term objective of the initiative is to build a united opposition force that could eventually become what they described as Sri Lanka\u2019s \u201cnext national team.\u201d"
