    "chunk_text": "Minister visits injured prison officers and inmates at National Hospital\n\nColombo, July 7 (Daily Mirror) - Health Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa today visited the National Hospital of Sri Lanka to review the condition of those injured in the recent unrest at the Negombo Prison.\n\nThe Minister met injured prison officers and inmates receiving treatment at Wards 72 and 79, as well as the Intensive Care Unit (ICU), and was briefed on their medical condition and the treatment being provided.\n\nHe also held discussions with hospital administrators, doctors, nursing staff and prison officials on the progress of treatment, immediate requirements and necessary support measures for the injured.\n\nAccording to the Health Ministry, 29 people injured during the Negombo Prison incident remain admitted to the NHSL, including 15 prison officers and 14 inmates.\n\nNo casualties among foreign inmates in Negombo prison clash: Authorities\n\nBodies of Negombo prison clash victims begin to be handed over to families"
