    "chunk_text": "QA\u2019s pivotal role in shaping future of AI-driven innovation highlighted\n\nSLASSCOM successfully concluded SLASSCOM Quality Summit 2026, held under the theme \u2018From Quality to Intelligence: QA\u2019s Role in the AI Revolution\u2019.\n\nThe two-day virtual summit brought together global experts, technology leaders and quality engineering professionals to explore the rapidly evolving role of quality assurance (QA) in an increasingly artificial intelligence (AI)-driven world.\n\nThe summit underscored how QA is moving beyond traditional testing functions to become a strategic discipline focused on trust, governance, intelligent automation and ethical AI adoption. This year\u2019s discussions strongly reflected the industry\u2019s growing need for QA professionals to play a central role in enabling responsible, reliable and scalable AI-powered innovation.\n\nThe event commenced with opening remarks from SLASSCOM Chairperson Shehani Senevirathne, who highlighted the importance of equipping the quality engineering community to navigate the next phase of transformation driven by AI.\n\nDay one featured a series of high-impact technical sessions. Ren\u00e9 van Veldhuijzen of SQUERIST delivered a session titled \u2018Shift Left, Shift Right, Stay Centered: Closing the Loop on Continuous Quality\u2019, emphasising modern quality engineering practices and the importance of embedding quality throughout the software development lifecycle.\n\nAdding further depth to the discussion, 99x Architect Test Automation Ruwanthi Soysa presented \u2018QA Strategies for Trustworthy AI Assisted Quality Engineering\u2019, offering insights into building reliable AI-assisted testing frameworks with transparency and control.\n\nMeanwhile, Capgemini Senior Test Automation Architect Neelam Pal addressed governance and ethics through her session \u2018Governance, Compliance and Ethical AI Assurance\u2019, highlighting the critical importance of accountability and compliance in AI-enabled systems."
