    "md5": "6097c4b7b627d666baf455400cbd8add",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "HNB General Insurance among SL\u2019s 50 Best Workplaces\n\nBecomes only general insurer named among Sri Lanka\u2019s 50 Best Workplaces 2026 by Great Place To Work\n\nHNB General Insurance (HNBGI) has become the only general insurance company to make it to the exclusive list of 50 Best Workplaces in Sri Lanka for 2026.\n\nCompiled by Great Place To Work, the renowned global authority on workplace culture, the prestigious list features 50 Sri Lankan organisations across all sizes, with HNBGI ranking 16th in the Large Sized Workplaces (>500 Employees) segment.\n\nThis recognition is based on comprehensive, confidential survey data assessing employee experiences of trust, innovation by all, meaningful organisational values and leadership effectiveness. Organisations were rigorously evaluated on how well they create a \u2018For All\u2019 workplace experience, where every single employee is welcomed, supported and engaged.\n\nAccording to Great Place To Work, \u201cA best workplace is one in which employees, no matter who they are and what they do for the organisation, are having a consistently positive experience of a \u2018Great Place To Work For All\u2019. It is an honour for HNB General Insurance to be recognised by their employees as an organisation that fosters a foundation of trust and meaningful values through effective leaders.\u201d\n\nHNBGI Executive Director and CEO Sithumina Jayasundara stated, \u201cTransitioning from being Certified last year to becoming the only general insurance company to be recognised among Sri Lanka\u2019s 50 Best Workplaces this year makes this achievement even more meaningful and reinforces our commitment to building a workplace where our people can thrive.\u201d\n\nHNBGI Vice President and Head of Human Resources Malsha Munasinghe said, \u201cEarning a spot on this prestigious list validates our long-term commitment to nurturing an environment where talent meets opportunity, completely free of barriers.\u201d"
  },
