    "chunk_text": "Little beauty powerhouse \u2026\n\nYes, tomatoes are full of lycopene, vitamin C, and natural acids that help brighten and clear skin, and amazing for the scalp, too.\n\nHere are some easy homemade beauty tips with tomatoes you can do right in your kitchen:\n\nMash the tomato, mix it with the honey and apply to clean face. Let it remain for 15 minutes, and then rinse with cool water.\n\n: Tomato brightens, while honey hydrates. Your skin will look fresh even on grey days.\n\nRub a slice of tomato gently on lips for 01 minute, before bed, and let the juice remain overnight. Rinse in the morning.\n\nPatch test first \u2013 if your skin is sensitive, test on your wrist.\n\nUse fresh tomatoes \u2013 and don\u2019t use if you have open cuts. The acid can sting.\n\nYou will need 01 big ripe tomato and 02 teaspoons of lemon juice.\n\nBlend the tomato and strain the juice. Mix in the lemon juice and apply directly to scalp with your fingers. Massage for 05 minutes, let it remain for 20 minutes, and then shampoo as usual.\n\nKills dandruff-causing fungus and soothes itching. Do this once a week.\n\nYou will need 01 tomato, 01 egg yolk and 01 teaspoon castor oil.\n\nBlend all together and apply to scalp and hair. Leave 30 minutes, then wash.\n\nProtein from egg and vitamins from tomato help strengthen roots. Do this every 10 days.\n\nImportant: Don\u2019t use on coloured hair \u2013 the acidity can fade colour a bit.\n\nAlways follow with conditioner \u2013 tomato can be drying if you skip this.\n\nSmell tip: The tomato smell goes away after one wash. Add a few drops of rosemary or lavender oil if you want.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
